ser":{"login":"williluk","id":146780724,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL-yNA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146780724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/williluk","html_url":"https://github.com/williluk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williluk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williluk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williluk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williluk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williluk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williluk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williluk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williluk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williluk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-16T01:20:44Z","updated_at":"2025-11-16T01:20:44Z","body":"I'm going to keep examining this, but it is possible that this is intended behavior. \n\nIn the spatial editor, the Ctrl / - keyboard shortcut is bound to \"Increase Field of View\" and in the orthogonal view the FOV could be used to control the size of the rectangle that will be rendered to the viewport (unsure if that is standard). This would be visually identical to zooming, but they are technically two functions.\n\nThis still means that the viewport settings tab doesn't respect setting FOV via keyboard shortcut, which is still probably worth fixing. \n\nAlso appears that the manual doesn't list this keyboard shortcut at all, so that's another issue.\n\nVery thankful if any maintainers let me know if this analysis is accurate. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3537280145/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"perf